From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 08:32:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: fail the WMAC bring-up when the A-die
 can't be read

mt798x_wmac_sku_setup() returned 0 even when reading an A-die's chip id
over SPI failed, so mt7986_wmac_enable() went on configuring the A-dies
and the SKU from its uninitialised adie_type.

Return the error. Un-skip mt7915_soc_test_sku_setup_error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt7915/soc.c            | 2 +-
 mt7915/tests/soc-test.c | 2 --
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7915/soc.c b/mt7915/soc.c
index da59412f..df89b61c 100644
--- a/mt7915/soc.c
+++ b/mt7915/soc.c
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ static int mt798x_wmac_sku_setup(struct mt7915_dev *dev, u32 *adie_type)
 out:
 	mt76_wmac_spi_unlock(dev);
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static inline u16 mt7986_adie_idx(u8 adie, u32 adie_type)
diff --git a/mt7915/tests/soc-test.c b/mt7915/tests/soc-test.c
index a0e7d81a..986b760d 100644
--- a/mt7915/tests/soc-test.c
+++ b/mt7915/tests/soc-test.c
@@ -905,8 +905,6 @@ static void mt7915_soc_test_sku_setup_error(struct kunit *test)
 	struct mt7915_soc_test *t;
 	u32 type = 0;
 
-	kunit_skip(test, "driver bug: mt798x_wmac_sku_setup() returns 0 when an A-die chip id read fails, and mt7986_wmac_enable() goes on with its uninitialized adie_type");
-
 	t = mt7915_soc_test_init(test, &dev);
 	t->spi_ok = 0;
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt798x_wmac_sku_setup(dev, &type), -ETIMEDOUT);
